hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"9571","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu Ubaid, the client of Sulayman bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “Whoever says Subhāh thirty-three times after every prayer, and says “Allahu Akbar” thirty-three times, and praises be to Him thirty-three times, and completes the hundred “There is no god but God” Alone, He has no partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. His sins are forgiven, even if they are like the foam of the sea.” Zayd bin Abi Unaisah narrated it, on the authority of Suhail, and said: On the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah."
"9572","Muhammad bin Wahb told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahim told me, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Unaisah, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “Whoever exalts God thirty-three times at the end of each prayer, says “Allahu Akbar” thirty-three times, and praises God thirty-three times, and says completely: There is no god but God, He alone has no partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise. He gives life and causes death, and He has power over all things. He is forgiven for whatever deeds he has done, even if they are more than “The foam of the sea.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The correct view is Abu Ubaid, the client of Suleiman bin Abd al-Malik. Ibn Ajlan disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yazid, on the authority of some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9573","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, On the authority of some of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever says after every prayer thirty-three takbirs, thirty-three tasbihs, and three And thirty praises and tahlilas, saying: There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things, He forgives. His sins are his, even if they are like the foam of the sea.” Adam bin Abi Iyas disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9574","Musa bin Sahl told us, he said: Adam told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says after every prayer thirty-three takbeers, thirty-three tasbihs, and thirty-three Praise, and he says: There is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things, His sins are forgiven. Even if it is like the foam of the sea.” It was narrated by Sumayyah, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, with another wording."
"9575","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir told us, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The poor came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: The people of wealth have gone from the wealth of the highest levels. And eternal bliss. They pray as we pray, and fast as we fast, and they have abundant wealth from which they perform Hajj and Umrah, and they strive. And they give in charity? He said: “Shall I not inform you of a matter which, if you adhere to it, you will overtake those who came before you, and no one will overtake you after you, and you will be the best among yourselves?” “Dhahrani, except for someone who did what you do?” Do you praise, praise, and glorify Allah thirty-three times after each prayer? Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’ disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, L6271, narrated by Jarir. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9576","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Darda’, he said I said: O Messenger of God, the people of wealth have pursued this world and the hereafter, praying as we pray, remembering as we remember, and striving as we do. We struggle, but we do not find anything to give in charity? He said: “Shall I not tell you something that, if you do it, you will catch up with those who came before you, and no one who came after you will catch up with you except those who said like what you said?” You glorify God thirty-three times at the end of every prayer, praise Him thirty-three times, and say “Allahu Akbar” thirty-four times. Sharik bin Abdullah disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Umar, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’"
"9577","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of a man from the people of the Levant who is said to be It is narrated by Abu Umar, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, who said: A guest came to Abu al-Darda’ and said to him: “Am I staying and let’s go, or are we going to forage and feed?” He said: Za’in. He said: I do not find anything to offer you better than something I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about. I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace and blessings of God be upon him. I said: O Messenger of God, the owners of wealth have gone with goodness. They fast as we fast, and they pray as we pray, and they give in charity, but not Do we have money that we can give in charity? He said: “O Abu Darda’, shall I not direct you to something that, if you did, no one before you could have preceded you, and no one after you could have overtaken you except those who He brought something similar to what you brought? Do you glorify God thirty-three times after every prayer, praise Him thirty-three times, and glorify Him thirty-four times?” Sufyan bin Saeed disagreed with them. He narrated it, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Omar al-Sinni, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’ (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9578","Bishr ibn Khalid informed us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Hisham informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Aziz ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Umar. Al-Sinni, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, said: I said: O Messenger of God, those who have money go to this world and the hereafter, praying, fasting, and striving. As we do, and they give in charity and we do not? He said: “Shall I not guide you to a matter which, if you adopted it, you would overtake those who came before you, and no one after you would overtake you except those who did the same as what you have done?” Glory be to God. After every prayer, you recite thirty-three times, you praise Him thirty-three times, and you say “Allahu Akbar” thirty-four times.” Shu'bah continued it and narrated it, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Omar Al-Sinni, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda'"
"9579","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of al-Hakam, he said: I heard Abu Omar al-Sinni, on the authority of my father Al-Darda', he said: I said: O Messenger of God, the rich have gone with the reward, they perform Hajj but we do not perform Hajj, they perform jihad but we do not perform jihad, and such and such, Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not guide you to something that, if you adopt it, you will come with better than what any of them brings? That you should say ‘Allahu Akbar’.” thirty-four times, and glorify Him thirty-three times, and praise Him thirty-three times at the end of every prayer.” Zaid bin Abi Unaisah disagreed with them. He narrated it, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Sinni, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9580","Muhammad bin Wahb told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahim told me, he said: Zaid told me, on the authority of Al-Hakam On the authority of Abu Amr Al-Sinni, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and some of them said: O Messenger of God, the The rich precede us in all good things. They pray as we pray, and fast as we fast, and they prefer us, so they give in charity, but we do not find anything to give in charity. And they spend in the way of God, but we find nothing with which to spend? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you of something that, if you do it, they will not have preceded you, nor will anyone after you realize it except those who did it?” Do you say “Allahu Akbar” thirty-three times after each prayer, “thanks” thirty-three times, and “Allahu Akbar” thirty-four times? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9581","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Musa al-Juhani, he said: I heard Musab bin Saad On the authority of Saad, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Is one of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds every day?” They said: O Messenger God, who can bear that? He said: “He says Allah a hundred times, and a thousand good deeds are recorded for him, and a thousand sins are erased from him.” Sufyan bin Saeed bin Masruq disagreed with him regarding the wording of the hadith."
"9582","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Arafah told us, he said: Al-Mubarak bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Musa, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, on the authority of Saad, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What prevents one of you from saying “Tasbih” ten times after every prayer, and saying “Allahu Akbar” ten times, And he praises ten times? That is in five prayers, fifty, a hundred in the tongue, and a thousand and five hundred in the scale, and when he goes to bed. He glorified God thirty-three times, and praised thirty-three times, and said “Allahu Akbar” thirty-four times. That is a hundred on the tongue, and a thousand on the scale. So which of you will do this? “In one thousand and five hundred bad days and nights?” Ya’la bin Ubaid disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Musa al-Juhani, on the authority of Musa, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah."
"9583","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ali told us, he said: Musa, who is Al-Juhani, told us, on the authority of Musa, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “Whoever says: At the end of every prayer there are ten tasbihs, ten takbeers, and ten praises, in five prayers, that is fifty.” And a hundred in the tongue, and a thousand and five hundred in the balance, and when he takes his bed for a hundred, that is a hundred in the tongue, and a thousand in the The scale, which of you will suffer two thousand and five hundred bad days?"
"9584","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Samra told us, on the authority of Asbat. He said: Amr bin Qais told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ujrah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They are repeated, and the one who says them will not be disappointed: He glorifies God three times after every prayer.” “And He praises Him thirty-three times, and He glorifies Him thirty-four times.” Endowed by Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9585","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ujrah said: “There are things that do not disappoint those who say them: He says ‘Tasbih’ thirty-three times after every prayer, and ‘Thanks’ thirty-three times, and he says ‘Allahu Akbar’ four times.” \And thirty\"""""""
"9586","Musa bin Hazzam told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Ibn Idris, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of many Ibn Aflah, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Thabit, said: “They were commanded to say “Tasbih” thirty-three times after each prayer, and to praise thirty-three times, and to say “Allahu Akbar” four times. And thirty-three. Then a man from the Ansar came in his dream, and it was said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded you to say “Tasbih” thirty-three times after every prayer. And praise them thirty-three times, and say “Allahu Akbar” thirty-four times. He said: Yes. He said: So make it twenty-five, and put in it the Tahlil. So when In the morning he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and that was mentioned to him, and he said: Make it that way.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9587","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, he said: Abu al-Jawab told us, he said: Ammar told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza, On the authority of Ata’ al-Khorasani, on the authority of Hamran, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Omar saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Who He said: Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is great. Ten good deeds were recorded for him for every letter. Ibrahim bin Tahman disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, his saying"
"9588","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman told us, on the authority of Ata al-Khurasani, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: “Whoever says: Glory be to God and praise be to Him, God will record for him ten, and whoever says ten, God will record for him a hundred.” And whoever says it a hundred times, God will record for him a thousand, and whoever increases it, God will increase it for him, and whoever asks for forgiveness, God will forgive him.” Raised by Matar bin Tahman Al-Warraq"
"9589","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Issa bin Shuaib told us, he said: Ruh bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Remember the servants of God, for when the servant says: Glory be to God and praise be to Him, God writes for him And from ten to a hundred, and from a hundred to a thousand, so whoever increases, God will increase for him, and whoever asks forgiveness, God will forgive him.”"
"9590","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, left his house when he prayed the morning prayer while Juwayriyah was sitting in the mosque, then he returned when daylight came and said: “Why? Are you still in your gathering? She said: Yes. He said: I said four words, then I repeated them three times. If they were weighed against what you said, I would weigh them: Glory be to God and praise be to Him, and there is no god but God, according to the number of His creation, His pleasure, the weight of His Throne, and the ink of His words.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9591","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, and the pronunciation for it, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Abdul told us Al-Rahman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The name of Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith was Burrah, so the Prophet changed it and prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. So he named her Juwayriyah, so he passed by her reading while she was in her place of prayer, praising God and remembering God. Then he passed by her after he rose. During the day, he said: “O Juwayriyah, are you still in your place?” She said: “I have been in my place since you learned.” He said: “I have spoken four things.” I repeated them three times, and they are better than what you said: Glory be to God according to the number of His creation, Glory be to God the beauty of His Throne, Glory be to God the ink of His words, And praise be to God for that.” It was narrated by Shu`bah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Juwayriyah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9592","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by Juwayriyah while she was in. He mentioned a place, then he passed by her close to noon, and said to her: “ Are you still here?” He said: “Shall I not teach you the words: Glory be to God, according to the number of His creations? He repeated them three times; Glory be to God, He is pleased with Himself, three times.” “Glory be to God, as beautiful as His Throne, three times. Glory be to God, the ink of His words, three times.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9593","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, the client of Abu Talha, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Juwayriyah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by her while she was in the mosque praying, then he passed by her close to The middle of the day, and he said to her: “Are you still in your condition?” She said: Yes, and he said: “Shall I not teach you?” And he mentioned a word that means words that you should say: Glory be to Him. God is the number of His creation, Glory be to God, He is pleased with Himself, Glory be to God, He is pleased with Himself, Glory be to God, He is pleased with Himself, Glory be to God, the weight of His throne, Glory be to God, the weight of His throne, Glory be to God, the weight of His throne, Glory be to God, the ink of His words, Glory be to God, the ink of His words, Glory be to God, the ink ""His words."" Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Mas’ar told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Rushdin On the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Juwayriyah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by her after the morning prayer while she was remembering God, then he returned and walked. Hadith. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Rishdin is Kuraib, the client of Ibn Abbas, and his son is Rashdin bin Kuraib Da’eef, and his brother Muhammad bin Kurayb is not strong except that he has reformed a little, and Kurayb is trustworthy, and there is no weak person among Ibn Abbas’s loyalists except Shu’bah, the client of Ibn Abbas. Malik, he said: He did not resemble the reciters. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9594","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, he said: Yahya bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan told me, On the authority of Musab bin Muhammad bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad bin Zurarah, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He passed by him while he was moving his lips, and he said: “What do you say, Abu Umamah?” He said: I remember my Lord. He said: “Shall I not tell you something better or more than Your remembrance of the night with the day and the day with the night, to say: Glory be to God, according to the number of what He created, Glory be to God, filling what He created, Glory be to God, according to the number of what is in The earth and the sky, Glory be to God, filling what is in the heavens and the earth, Glory be to God, filling what He created, Glory be to God, as many as His Book has counted, and Glory be to God Filling everything, and saying: Praise be to God like that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9595","Amr bin Uthman and Issa bin Musawar informed us, saying: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Ala, and Ibn Jabir, saying: Abu Salam, on the authority of Abu Salma, the shepherd of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Bakh, blah, what The heaviest in the scale: There is no god but God, Glory be to God, praise be to God, God is great, and the righteous servant dies as a Muslim. So he thinks he will do it.”"
"9596","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Aban, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ash’ari, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Praise be to God, it fills the scale, and there is no god but God, and God is great, it fills “Between the sky and the earth.” Muawiyah bin Salam disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of his brother Zaid, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanam, on the authority of Abu Malik (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9597","Issa bin Musawar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salam, on the authority of his brother, he told him, on the authority of his grandfather, Abu Salam, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanam, that Abu Malik al-Ash’ari narrated to him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Praise be to God, it is filled with The scales, and glorification and glorification fill the heavens and the earth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9598","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, and another mentioned, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, he said: I said to Jabir bin Samurah: Were you sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “Yes, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed Fajr, he would sit in his place of prayer until the sun rose, and his companions would talk and remember.” Hadith of pre-Islamic times, and they sing poetry and laugh, and he smiles.”"
"9599","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Omar passed by Hassan bin Thabit. While he was singing in the mosque, he noticed him and said: I sang there, and there is someone better than you. Then he turned to Abu Hurairah and said: Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Answer on my behalf, O God, support him with the Holy Spirit”? He said: Yes. Shuaib bin Abi Hamza disagreed with him"
"9600","Imran bin Bakkar told me, he said: Abu Al-Yaman told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah bin told me. Abdul Rahman, that he heard Hassan bin Thabit, citing Abu Hurairah as a martyr: I adjure you by God, did you hear the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “O Hassan, answer on behalf of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Oh God, support him with the Holy Spirit”? Abu Hurairah said: Yes (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9601","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, “that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade reciting poems in the mosque.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9602","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan al-Shaybani, he said: Alqamah bin Marthad told me, On the authority of Suleiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man say: Whoever calls for the red camel in the mosque, He said: “No, I did not find it, but these mosques were built for the one for whom they were built.” Mis’ar bin Kadam disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Buraidah, with a mursal message. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9603","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, On the authority of Ibn Buraydah: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man praying for a lost woman in the mosque, and he said: No, I found her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9604","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Ali bin Al-Madini told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusayfa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Thawban, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you see someone selling or... He makes purchases in the mosque, so say: May God not make you profit from your trade. And if you see someone seeking a lost item in the mosque, say: May God not bring you back. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9605","Suleiman bin Ubaid Allah told us, he said: Abu Amer told us, he said: Suleiman told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Saeed, He said: I heard Abu Humaid and Abu Usayd saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you enters the mosque, let him say: Oh God, open the doors of your mercy for me, and when he leaves, let him say: Oh God, I ask you of your grace.”"
"9606","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Jabir, that he heard the Prophet praying May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “If a man enters his house and mentions God when he enters it and when he eats food, Satan says: There is no place for you to stay, nor He had dinner here, and when he entered and did not mention God, Satan said: Have you spent the night? But if he did not mention God when he ate, Satan said: “You have spent the night and dinner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9607","Ahmad ibn Amr told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr informed me, and someone else before him mentioned, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, that he heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas: that Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq said: O Messenger of God, teach me a supplication that I may pray with in my prayers. And in my house? He said: “Say: O God, I have wronged myself greatly, and no one can forgive sins except You, so grant me forgiveness from You, and have mercy on me. “You are the Forgiving, the Merciful.”"
"9608","Ibrahim bin Saeed Al-Jawhari told us, he said: Al-Ahwas bin Jawab told us, on the authority of Sa’ir bin Al-Khams, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is shown a kindness and says to the one who did it: May God reward you.” Good, for he has conveyed the praise most eloquently.”"
"9609","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Bahrani told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, He said: The emigrants said: O Messenger of God, the Ansar went with the entire reward. We have never seen a people better in giving to many, nor better Consolation for a few of them, and they have provided us with sufficient supplies? He said: “Aren’t you praising them for it, and praying to God for them?” They said: Yes, he said: “So that for that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9610","Muhammad bin Aqeel Al-Naysaburi told me, he said: Ali bin Al-Hussein, who is Ibn Waqid, told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Thabit, he said: Anas bin Malik told me, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man passed by, and a man from among the people said: Oh Prophet of God, by God, I love this man. He said: “Did you inform him of that?” He said: No. He said: “Get up and teach him.” So he got up to him and said: “O This, by God, I love you. He said: The one for whom you loved me loved you. Hammad bin Salamah disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9611","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Habib Ibn Abi Subayah al-Dhabi’i, on the authority of al-Harith, that a man was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man passed by him and said: O Messenger of God, I love him for the sake of God. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Did you not teach him that?” He said: No. He said: “Then go to him and teach him.” So he went to him and said: I love you for the sake of God. He said: The one for whom you loved me loved you. Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Al-Hajjaj told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Subayah, On the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of a man who told him this hadith. Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is correct according to us, and the hadith of Hussein bin Waqid is wrong, and Hammad bin Salama has been proven, and God knows best, with a proven hadith from Hussein bin Waqid, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9612","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Bishr bin al-Mufaddal told us, he said: Humayd told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Awf came to us, Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a brotherhood between him and Sa’d bin al-Rabi’, and Sa’d said to him: I am one of the most wealthy Ansar, so I will share my wealth with you. Half, and I have two wives, so I divorce one of them, and when her waiting period has expired, he can marry her. He said: May God bless your family and your wealth. “Show me to the market.” When he returned from the market that day, he picked up some wheat and ghee, and brought it to the house. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9613","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, he said: I was a companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and there was only the end of the journey between me and him. He said: “O Muadh,” so I said: At your service, O Messenger of God. And Saadik, he said: “Do you know what God’s right is upon His servants?” I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “God’s right upon His servants is that they worship Him and not They associate anything with Him.” Then he said: “O Muadh bin Jabal.” I said: At your command, O Messenger of God, and I am pleased with you. He said: “Do you know what the servants’ right is upon me?” By God, if they did that? I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: Their right upon him is that he should not torture them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9614","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Bishr, he said: Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told us, he said: Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hatib, who said: I took a pot that I had and my hands were burned, so my mother took me to a man sitting in the cemetery. She said to him: O Messenger of God, he said: “I am at your service and I am pleased with you.” Then she brought me closer to him, and he began to spit and speak words that I do not know what they are. So I asked my mother after that what he was saying. She said: He was saying: “Remove the afflicted, Lord of the people. Heal, You are the healer. There is no healer but You.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9615","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, entered the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said to him: How are you, O Messenger of God? He said: “A righteous person is a man who has not fasted in the morning, is no longer sick, and has not followed a funeral.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Omar bin Abi Salamah is not strong in hadith."
"9616","Muhammad bin Al-Ala Abu Kurayb told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out with his companions, so we went out with him and entered ihram for Hajj. When we approached Mecca, he said: “Who has not If he has a sacrificial animal with him, let him make it an Umrah, for had I not had a sacrificial animal with me, I would have permissible.” Then he said: When there was nothing between us and him except that, and he We entered ihram for Hajj, so how do we make it Umrah? He said: “Look at what I command you and do it.” He said: They responded to him and he became angry, then he set off until he entered upon Aisha in anger, and she saw Anger appeared on his face, so she said: Whoever makes you angry, God will make him angry. So he said: Why should I not get angry when I command the matter and it is not followed? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9617","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr informed us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad ibn Al-Had said: I heard Ali saying: “I did not hear the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, unite his parents for anyone except Saad.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9618","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Ali, he said: What I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ransom someone other than Saad, and I heard him say: “Throw it away, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9619","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Ali He said: I did not see the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathering his parents for anyone except Saad, for he said: “Throw, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9620","Sulayman bin Matar al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jud’an, on the authority of Sa’id, who is Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ali, he said I have never seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gather his parents together for anyone other than himself, meaning Saad. He said to him on the day of Uhud: “Throw, may my father be sacrificed for you.” And my mother"
"9621","Ibrahim bin Saeed Al-Jawhari told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ali, He said: “I have never heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, unite his parents for anyone other than Saad.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9622","Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Sa’d said: The Messenger of God has gathered for me May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the day of the death of both of his parents. He meant a time. He said: “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you,” while he was fighting."
"9623","Ali bin Khashram told us, he said: Isa told us, he is Ibn Yunus, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered his parents for me on the day of Uhud and said: “Am, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is what is correct according to us, and the hadith of Sufyan is an error, and God knows best."
"9624","Muhammad bin Khalil told us, on the authority of Marwan bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Hashim, who is the son of Hashim bin Hashim bin Utbah, he said: I heard Saeed Ibn Al-Musayyab, saying: I heard Saad, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took his quilt on the day of Uhud, and said: “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9625","Al-Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Amr bin Muhammad told us, he said: Bukayr bin Mismar told us, he said: I heard Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Uhud while he was handing him an arrow: “Aim, may my father be sacrificed for you.” “And my mother,” he said: “I shot a man from the polytheists and knocked him down.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: The narration of Al-Layth and Isa bin Yunus is more worthy of authenticity in our view than the hadith of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9626","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abdah bin Sulayman informed us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Urwa, On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered his parents for me on the day of Qurayza, and he said: “By my father’s ransom.” And my mother"
"9627","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of al-Zubayr, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered his parents for me on the day of Uhud.”"
"9628","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Makhrami told us, he said: Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, he said: “I and Omar bin Abi Salamah were on the day of the ditch, and it was He would bow down to me and I would look at the fighting, then I would bow down to him and he would look at the fighting. One day I saw Al-Zubayr riding around in the swamp on his horse. So I said to him: Father, I saw you roaming in the marsh on your horse? He said: And you saw me? I said: Yes, he said: As for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? “And he greeted his parents for me today.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9629","Yunus bin Abdullah Al-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Al-Mundhir bin Abdullah Al-Hazami told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the Day of the Trench, gathered his parents for Al-Zubayr and said: May I be sacrificed for you.” \My father and my mother\"""""""
"9630","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Jafar, saying: I heard Ismail bin Muhammad, he said: Abu Yazid was in his chain of transmission. Abdullah bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad, On the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Uhud, saying: “Strike Sa’ad, shoot, shoot.” God is yours, shoot, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9631","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim Al-Awdi told us, he said: Zakaria bin Adi told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Abdul Rahman bin Saad bin Makhramah, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Uhud to my father: “Strive, Sa’d. Shoot, O Sa’d. May God shoot for you. Shoot, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9632","Ahmad bin Bakkar Al-Harrani told me, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Khabbab, he said: Ikrimah told me, he said: I was accompanying him and Saeed bin Jubayr, and he said: Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Asi said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “When you see people whose covenants have been broken, their trusts betrayed, and they are like this.” He interlaced his fingers, and I stood up to him. So I said to him: What should I do then, O Messenger of God, may God make me your ransom? He said: “Stay at home, keep your tongue in check, take what you know, and leave what you deny, and you are responsible for a matter that is only for yourself, and leave a matter for yourself.” \public\"""""""
"9633","Shuaib bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Thawr, he said: Habib bin Ubaid narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karib, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you loves his brother, let him know that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9634","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Had, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad, On the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Abdul Rahman bin Zayd, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, On the authority of his father, he said: Omar asked permission to go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and there were women from Quraysh with him who were talking to him and asking him to talk to him a lot. With their voices, when Omar asked for permission, they hastened to veil, so Omar entered and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughing, so Omar said: May God make your years laugh. O Messenger of God, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I was amazed at these women who were with me. When they heard your voice, they hastened to hide.” Omar said: And you were more deserving that they should attack. Then Omar said: That is, the enemies of themselves, did you attack me and did not attack the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? And peace be upon him? They said: Yes, you are harsher and more vulgar than the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul.” Satan never meets you in a way other than yours.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9635","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri and al-Harith ibn Miskin informed us of a recitation by him while I was listening and his pronunciation, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: Amer passed by Sahl ibn Hunaif while he was bathing, and he said: I have never seen any skin like today. Hidden, he soon stumbled upon it, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was said: Sahl caught up with it, so he said: “Who are you accusing?” They said: Amer. Ibn Rabi’ah said: “Why should one of you kill his brother? If he sees something that he likes, let him pray for blessings,” and he ordered him to perform ablution and wash himself. He turned his face and hands to the elbows, knees, and inside his garment, then he ordered it to be poured. Al-Harith added: He went with the caravan. Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl, on the authority of His father, that Amer passed by him while he was washing, and the like. Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Uthman bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, on the authority of Amer bin Rabi’ah, that he saw Sahl bin Hunaif while he was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Jiranah, bathing. So he mentioned something similar. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ja`far ibn Burqan is weak in al-Zuhri, but in other matters there is no harm in him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9636","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, On the authority of Umayyah ibn Hind, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Aamir ibn Rabi’ah, on the authority of his father, he said: Sahl ibn Hunaif and I went out and found a cave. One of us was ashamed for anyone to see him, so he hid himself from me, until when he saw that he had done so, he took off his cloak and entered the water, and I looked at him carefully. I liked his behavior, so I struck him with an eye, and he started to rattle. I called him, but he did not answer me. So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I told him the news, and he said: “Come with us.” So he came to him and raised his leg, as if I could see the whiteness and clarity of his leg as he waded through the water. So he came to him and said: “O God, remove her freedom and give her a bath.” Then he said: “Get up.” So he stood up, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When he saw If any of you likes himself, or his wealth, or his brother, let him pray for blessing.”"
"9637","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of his brother Issa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “If one of you sneezes Let him say: Praise be to God in every condition, and respond to them: May God have mercy on you, and respond to them: May God forgive us and you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9638","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Sa’id bin Amir told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of his father On the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The one who sneezes says: Praise be to God in every situation, and the one who sneezes at him says: May God have mercy on you, and say to him: May God guide you and put your mind at ease.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila is not strong in hadith and has poor memory, and he is one of the jurists. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9639","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Sneezing is from God, and yawning is from Satan, so if one of you sneezes Let him praise God, and it is right for everyone who heard him to say: May God have mercy on you.”"
"9640","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Sa’id Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God loves sneezing, and hates yawning, so if one of you sneezes, let him thank God.” It is the duty of whoever heard it to say: May God have mercy on you. As for yawning, it is only from Satan. So if one of you yawns Let him repel it as much as he can, for if one of you says: Ha-ha-ha, Satan laughs at him.” Al-Qasim bin Yazid Al-Jarmi disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9641","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Al-Qasim told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God loves sneezing and hates yawning, so if one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to God. And whoever heard him must say: May God have mercy on you. As for yawning, it is only from Satan, so if one of you yawns, let him repeat it. As much as he is able, for if one of you yawns and says: Ha-ha, Satan laughs at him.”"
"9642","Muhammad ibn Adam told us, on the authority of Abu Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Sneezing is from God, and yawning is from Satan. So when one of you yawns, do not say: Ha, ha, for Satan laughs at me.” \His stomach\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9643","Siwar bin Abdullah bin Siwar told us, he said: Safwan bin Issa told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhubab told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abu Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When God created Adam and breathed into him the spirit, he sneezed and thanked his Lord.” With God’s permission for him, he said: Praise be to God. Then his Lord said to him: Your Lord has mercy on you, O Adam. Go to those leaders, and a crowd of them was seated. Then say: Peace be upon you. They said: May God’s peace and mercy be upon you. Then he returned to his Lord and said: This is your greeting and the greeting of your descendants among them. \. Muhammad bin Ajlan disagreed with him in this regard (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9644","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, he said: “God created Adam in the last hour of Friday, then breathed into him of His spirit. When the spirit overtook him, he sneezed, and God Almighty said to him: Say: Praise be to God, and he said: Praise be to God, and God said: Your Lord has mercy on you, then he said to him: Go to the people of this council from The angels and greeted them. He did so and said: This is your greeting and the greeting of your descendants.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is the correct one, and the other is wrong, and the following is the hadith of Muhammad bin Khalaf, which is objectionable. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9645","Muhammad bin Khalaf told us, he said: Adam told us, he said: Abu Khaled Suleiman bin Hayyan told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told me, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Khaled said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Khaled said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind told me, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Khaled said: Ibn Abi Dhubab told me, he said: Sa’id al-Maqbari and Yazid bin Hurmuz told me, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “God created Adam with His own hand, and breathed into him of His spirit, and commanded the angels and they prostrated themselves before him.” So he sat down and sneezed and said: Praise be to God. Then his Lord said to him: May God have mercy on you, your Lord. Go to those angels and say: Peace be upon you. So he came to them. He said: Peace be upon you. They said to him: May the peace and mercy of God be upon you. Then he returned to his Lord Almighty and said to him: This is your greeting and the greeting of Your descendants are among them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9646","Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Ibn Shihab told me, that Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab told him On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The rights of a Muslim upon another Muslim are five: returning the greeting, and returning the greeting.” The sick, attending funerals, responding to someone who supplicates, and praising the one who sneezes.”"
"9647","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamar bin Sulaiman informed us, he said: I heard my father, saying: Anas bin Malik informed us, Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: Two men sneezed. In the presence of the Prophet, you smelled one of them and left the other. They said: O Messenger of God, two men sneezed in your presence, and you smelled one of them and left the other? He said: “This man praised God, and this man did not praise God.” The word is for Imran (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9648","Humayd bin Masada informed us, on the authority of Sulaym, who is Ibn Akhdar, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah, on the authority of his father, He said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man sneezed and I smelled him, then the second time he sneezed and said: “He has a cold.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9649","Al-Fadl bin Sahl Al-Araj told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Raqqashi told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “If one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to Him.” To God, Lord of the worlds, and it is said to him: May God have mercy on you, and when it is said to him: May God have mercy on you, he should say: May God forgive you. Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith, and I do not see Jafar bin Sulaiman except that he heard it from Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib after the mingling, and Ata’ entered Ibn Al-Sa'ib went to Basra twice, so whoever heard from him the first time, his hadith is authentic, and whoever heard from him the last time, there is something in his hadith, and Hammad Ibn Zaid’s hadith is authentic (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9650","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, he said: We were with Salim bin Ubaid on a travel, Then a man from among the people sneezed and said: Peace be upon you. Then he said: Peace be upon you and your mother. Then he said: Perhaps you recognized what I told you. I only told you As the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man from among the people sneezed and said: Peace be upon him. On you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “On you and your mother.” Then he said: “When one of you sneezes, let him thank God.” He mentioned some Al-Muhammad: “And let those who are with him say: May God have mercy on you, and let him respond to them: May God forgive us and you.” Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Ubaid Allah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Salem bin Ubaid. , like that (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9651","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Ahmad told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Salem Ibn Ubaid, he said: The Prophet said: “When one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds, and let whoever responds to him say to him: May God have mercy on you.” And let him say: May God forgive me and you.” Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Qasim told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of one man, on the authority of another, He said: We were with Salem bin Ubaid on a travel, and he said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man sneezed, like him. Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is correct according to us, and the first is wrong, and God knows best. Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of a man On the authority of Khalid bin Arafatah, on the authority of Salem bin Ubaid, he said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man sneezed, so he mentioned something similar. Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Yazid told us, and he is the son of Harun, he said: Warqa’ told us, on the authority of Mansour, On the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Khalid bin Arafatah, that they were walking with Salim bin Ubaid, so he mentioned something like this. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9652","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Yahya bin Hassan told us, he said: Abdul Aziz, who is Al-Majishun, told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin A dinar, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to God.” Lord, and let his brother or friend say to him: May God have mercy on you, and let him say: May God guide you and set your mind right.”"
"9653","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Hakam al-Warraq told me, he said: Muadh told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hakim ibn al-Daylam, on the authority of Abu Burdah. On the authority of Abu Musa, he said: Jews used to come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they would sneeze, hoping that he would say: May God have mercy on you, and it was He says: “May God guide you and set your mind right.”"
"9654","Suleiman bin Dawud informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwa informed me, On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and addressed the people, and said: “O community of Muslims, what is the matter with people? They stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of God. Whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of God, and if he stipulates a hundred times, it is not for him. God’s condition is more deserving. \And I bind\"""""""
"9655","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, granted permission in some matter, but some men refused to do so, so he said: “What is the matter with the men who command them?” Of the matter they turn away from, I know them best about God, and I strengthen them in fear of Him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9656","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Salam al-Alawi, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik narrating, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rarely confronts a man with something that he dislikes. He said: One day a man entered upon him bearing traces of the creatures, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He was eating squash, and he liked the squash. When the man came out, he said: If you command this man to wash it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9657","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Sulayman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Salam al-Alawi, on the authority of Anas: A man entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions were with him, bearing traces of yellowness. When he got up, he said to one of his companions: “If “You ordered this man to leave this man alone.” He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not confront anyone with anything."
"9658","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Maimun, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Masruq On the authority of Aisha, she said: A man passed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Wretched is Abdullah and the brother of the clan.” Then he entered upon him. I saw him approaching him with his face as if he had a status with him."
"9659","Muhammad bin Nasr told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, he said: Hatim told us, on the authority of Ibn Harmala, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nayyar, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that a man asked permission to come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he heard his voice, he said: “Wretched is the man, wretched.” “The son of the clan.” When he entered, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited to him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9660","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I heard Khaled talking, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that they mentioned a man with him, and a man said: O Messenger of God, there is no man After the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, better than him, and such and such. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Woe to you, you cut the neck of your companion.” He repeatedly said that, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you inevitably praises his brother, let him say: I consider so-and-so, He thought that he was like that, and I do not praise anyone before God, and God is his judge. I consider him to be such and such.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9661","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan told us, he said: Amr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you buys a female slave, or a boy, or an animal, let him take the forelock from it.” And let him say: O God, I ask You for its goodness and the goodness of what it was created with, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what it was created for. And if he buys a camel Let him take the top of his hump and say something like that.”"
"9662","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, who is Ibn Ja`far, he said: Al-Ala told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “None of you should say: My servant and my female slave. All of you are servants of God, and all of your women are God’s handmaids, but rather: My servant.” And my maidservant, and my sons, and my maidens.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9663","Muhammad bin Al-Ala Abu Kurayb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Let none of you say: My servant, for all of you are servants, but let him say: My boy, and let none of you say: My master. For your master is God, but let him say: “My master.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9664","Muhammad bin Khalaf Al-Asqalani told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Bilal told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ayyub and Hisham, And Habib, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should say: My servant and my nation. And the slave should not say: My Lord and my Lord, but let the owner say: My boy and my girl, and the slave: My master and my lady, for you are the slaves, and the Lord. God Almighty” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9665","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, On the authority of his father, the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not say to the hypocrite, ‘Our master,’ for if he is your master, then you have become displeased.” Your Lord (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9666","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Mutarrif, on the authority of his father, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: You are the master of Quraysh. He said: “Master God.” He said: You are the best of us in speech, and the greatest of us. There is a length in it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let each one of you say what he says, and not let Satan or the devils drag him down.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9667","Harami bin Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Mahdi bin Maymun told us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of his father, said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a group of Banu Amir, and we greeted him, and they said: You are our father, you are our master, you are the most excellent of us, and you are the longest over us, so he said: “Say what you say, no.” ""The devils tempt you."" Humayd bin Masada told us, on the authority of Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal, he said: Abu Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Mutarrif, he said: He said My father: I set out with a delegation from Bani Amer to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said: You are our master. He said: “Master God.” They said: And the best of us in virtue, so he mentioned something similar to it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9668","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, And Humayd, on the authority of Anas, that a man said: O Muhammad, O our master and the son of our master, the best of us and the son of the best of us, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “O people, speak what you say, and do not let the devils tempt you. I am Muhammad bin Abdullah, I am the servant of God and His Messenger. “And I do not like for you to raise me above the station that God has sent me down.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9669","Abu Bakr bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, that people They said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: O our best and the son of our best, and our master and the son of our master. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O people, adhere to what you say and do not let Satan tempt you. I do not want you to raise me above the station that God Almighty has sent me down. “I am Muhammad bin Abdullah, His servant and Messenger.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9670","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Muhammad bin Salih Al-Madani told me, he said: Muslim bin Abi told me Maryam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, who said: We were sitting with Abu Hurairah, when Hassan bin Ali bin Abi Talib came and greeted us, and we returned. And Abu Hurairah did not know, so he went on, so we said: Oh Abu Hurairah, this is Hassan bin Ali who greeted us, so he got up and followed him, and said: Oh My lord, so we said to him: You say: oh my lord? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “He is a master.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9671","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he addressed the people, and Al-Hasan bin Ali went up to him, hugged him to his chest and kissed him, and said: “This son of mine is a master, and he May God reconcile the two groups through him.”"
"9672","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu Musa told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan, saying: I heard Abu Bakra, He says: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the pulpit and Al-Hasan was with him, and he turned to the people once and to him once, and he said: “Indeed This son of mine is a gentleman, and perhaps God will bring about great reconciliation through him between two groups of Muslims.” Shaggy disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9673","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, meaning Anas, said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivering the sermon with Al-Hasan bin Ali on his thigh, and saying: “I hope That this son of mine will be a master, and I hope that God will reconcile two groups of my nation through him.” He was sent by Auf, Daoud, and Hisham. Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: I was informed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him. He said to Al-Hasan bin Ali, something like mursal. Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Dawud Al-Hafari told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him to Al-Hasan: “This son of mine is a master,” and the like. Muhammad bin Al-Ala Abu Kurayb told us, he said: Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “This son of mine is a master” and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9674","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Affan told us, he said: Abdul Wahid told us, he said: Uthman bin Hakim told us, he said: My grandmother Al-Rabbab told me, on the authority of Sahl ibn Hanif, who said: A torrent passed us, so we went to wash in it, and I came out with a fever, and it developed into The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Tell Abu Thabit to seek refuge,” so I said: Oh my lord, is the ruqyah valid? He said: “There is no ruqyah except for three reasons: fever, breath, and a bite.”"
"9675","Abdul-Ala bin Wasil bin Abdul-Ala informed us, saying: Malik bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Humaid, he said: Abd al-Karim bin Salit al-Basri told us. And Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Malik bin Ismail told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Humaid al-Rawasi told us, he said: he told us Abd al-Karim bin Salit, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that a group of Ansar said to Ali: You have Fatima, so he entered upon the Prophet and prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: “What is the need of Ibn Abi Talib?” He said: Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was mentioned. He said: “Hello and welcome.” He did not say anything more, so he went out to the group of Ansar who were waiting for him. They said: What is behind you? He said: I do not know except that he said to me: “Hello and welcome.” They said: One of them from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is sufficient for you. He gave you The family, and he gave you a welcome, and when he was after that, after he married him off, he said: “O Ali, the wedding must have a banquet,” Saad said: I have a ram, and a group of supporters gathered for it with a handful of corn. When it was the night of construction, he said: “O Ali, do not say anything until you meet me.” So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for water and performed ablution with it, then he poured it on Ali, and said: “O God, bless them both, and bless them.” And bless them in their young ones.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9676","Abdul Rahman bin Ubayd Allah Al-Halabi told us, saying: Al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Hurairah, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, showed compassion to a man, he would say: “May God bless you, and bless you, and bring you together in \Good\"""""""
"9677","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a slave The Most Gracious traced a whistle and said: “What is this?” He said: I married a woman worth the weight of a stone of gold. He said: “May God bless you, am I not?” Even with a sheep.”"
"9678","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, that Abd al-Rahman bin Awf married A woman from the Ansar, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met him and said: “Mahim?” He said: I married a woman, so he said: “Do I know, even if \With sheep\"""""""
"9679","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Aqeel bin Abi married He asked for a woman from Banu Jashm, and he was told: With prosperity and children. So he said: Say as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God bless among you, and bless you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9680","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Saeed, who is the son of Abi Ayyub, told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan told me, on the authority of Amr ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “If he informs If one of you sees a woman, or a servant, or a camel, let him put his hand on her forelock, then say: O God, I ask You for the best of her, and the best of what You have created for her. upon him, and I seek refuge in You from its evil, and from the evil of what You created it with. As for the camel, it takes the top of its hump and says something like that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9681","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Al-Mughirah Al-Yashkari, on the authority of Al-Ma'roor, on the authority of Abdullah, said: Umm Habibah said: O God, grant me the pleasure of my husband, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and my father's family. Sufyan, and with my brother Muawiyah, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “I prayed to God for specified times and known effects. And divided livelihoods, none of which advances before its appointed time, and nothing is delayed after its appointed term. If you ask God to protect you from the torment of Hellfire and the torment of the grave would be better for you.” Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi told us, he said: Khaled bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Al-Mustawirid bin Al-Ahnaf, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, and the like (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9682","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Mansour bin al-Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Salem Ibn Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you goes to his family He said: In the name of God, O God, spare us Satan and spare Satan from those whom You have provided for us. If a child is decreed between them in that, it will not harm him. Satan is never born.” Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Ghazwan, who is Ibn Abi Rizmah, informed us, saying: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said something similar. Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: Ibn Abi Umar told us, he said: Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, raising it to Ibn Abbas said. And Suleiman bin Ubaid Allah told us, he said: Bahz told us, 25 he said: Shu`bah told us, Mansour said, and Sulayman told me, on the authority of Salem, On the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If one of you goes to his family...”, he said Shu'bah: Solomon did not refer it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. It was narrated by Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Samad, on the authority of Suleiman (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9683","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Sulayman told us, on the authority of Salem bin Abi al-Ja’d, On the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a man comes to his family, he says: In the name of God, Oh God, spare us Satan, and spare Satan what You have bestowed upon us, for if a child is destined between them in that, that child will not be harmed by Satan.”"
"9684","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Abdul-Aziz bin Suhayb told us, he said: Anas bin Malik said: He built The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought Zainab bint Jahsh, and I sent a caller for food, so I called and the people would come and eat and leave. Then the people come and eat and leave, so I said: O Prophet of God, I have prayed until I find no one to invite, so he said: “Raise your food.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out and went to Aisha’s room and said: “Peace be upon you, people of the household.” They said: And peace be upon you, oh Messenger of God, how did you find your family? Then he came to his wives’ chambers, and they said the same as Aisha said. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9685","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: “Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, know when he built With Zainab, he satisfied the Muslims with bread and meat, then he went out to the mothers of the believers and greeted them, and they greeted him, and they prayed for him, and it was He will do this on the morning of its construction.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9686","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of Abu Hudhayfah, on the authority of Hudhayfah said: When we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we were invited to a meal and we did not lay down our hands until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat down. peace be upon him, so we were invited to a meal, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not lay down his hand, so we folded our hands, and a Bedouin came as if He was thrown out, so he leaned toward the bowl with his hand, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took his hand and made him sit down. Then a maid came and he fell down. with her hand to the bowl, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it by the hand, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The devil when Weary of us abandoning the mention of the name of God on our food, he brought this Bedouin deeming our food permissible, so when we imprisoned him he brought this slave girl. Our food is lawful with it, and by God, his hand is in my hand, along with her hand.” Then he mentioned the name of God and ate."
"9687","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, he heard it from Omar bin Abi Salamah, he said: I was a boy in the lap of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and my hand was wandering over the page, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Oh! Boy, name God, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what follows you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9688","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar Ibn Abi Salamah, that he entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was eating, and he said: “Come and eat.” In the name of God, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what follows you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9689","Abdullah bin Al-Sabbah bin Abdullah told us, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah, that he entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had food, and he said: “Come near, my son, and eat food.” God, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what follows you.”"
"9690","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abu Wajza, a man from Banu Saad, on the authority of a man from Muzainah, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Salamah, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O my son, when you eat, swear by God, and eat with your right hand, and eat \From what follows you\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9691","Muhammad ibn Adam told me, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abu Jazza al-Saadi, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Omar ibn Abi Salamah, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one day while he was eating. He said: “Sit down, my son, and give the name of God, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what follows you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9692","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Kathir told us, he said: I heard Wahb bin Kaysan, saying: I heard Omar bin Abi Salamah say: I was a boy in the lap of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and my hand was wandering over the paper, so the Prophet said to me: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “O boy, name God, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what follows you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9693","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Abu Nu’aym Wahb bin Kaysan, on the authority of Omar Ibn Abi Salama, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Name God, and eat of what follows you.” Qutaybah disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9694","Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Abu Nu’aym Wahb bin Kaysan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought. With food, and with him was his stepson, Omar bin Abi Salamah, and he said to him: “Name God, and eat of what follows you.”"
"9695","Abdullah bin Al-Sabbah bin Abdullah told us, saying: Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulayman told us, saying: I heard Hisham Abu Bakr, saying: Badil told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid, on the authority of a woman among them called Umm Kulthum, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, was eating in his house, then a hungry Bedouin came and ate him in two mouthfuls, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he had mentioned the name of God is sufficient for you. When one of you eats, let him mention the name of God. If he forgets to mention the name of God at the beginning, let him say: In the name of God at the beginning. And at the end of it \"" 9696"""""
"9696","'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Jabir ibn Subh narrated to us, saying: Muthanna ibn 'Abdur-Rahman al-Khuza'i narrated to me, saying: Umayyah ibn Makhshi narrated to us—and he was from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)—that the Prophet (ﷺ) saw a man eating without mentioning Allah's name (saying Bismillah). When he was at his last morsel, he said: ""In the name of Allah, at its beginning and its end."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The devil continued eating with him, but when he mentioned Allah's name, the devil vomited what he had eaten."""""
"9697","Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Baqiya told us, he said: Al-Sari bin Yanam told me, he said: Aamir bin Jashayb told me, he said: he told me Khaled bin Maadan. And Ahmad bin Yusuf told us, he said: Abu Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Al-Sari bin Yan’am Al-Jilani told us, he said: Aamir bin Jushayb told me. On the authority of Khaled bin Maadan, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: He was the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Amr said: He was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When he is satisfied with food, he greets him and says: “Praise be to God, abundant, good and blessed praise be to Him, neither rejected nor rejected.” Ahmad said: “It is neither sufficient nor dispensable with it.” The pronunciation is for Ahmad (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9698","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would raise his table, he would say: “Praise be to God abundantly, good and blessed, not sufficient or Our Lord is free of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9699","Yunus bin Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Sa`id bin Abi Ayyub told me, on the authority of Abu Aqeel al-Qurashi, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubali, on the authority of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that if he ate or drank, he said: “ Praise be to God who fed and watered it, made it easy and made a way out for it.”"
"9700","Ahmad bin Nasih told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ali bin Zaid told us, he said: Omar bin Abi Harmala told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever God Almighty feeds with food, let him say: O God, feed us with something better than it. And whoever is given milk to drink by God, let him say: O God, bless it for us and increase it, for there is nothing sufficient for food or drink other than milk.” Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, he said: I heard Omar bin Abi Harmala, He said: I heard Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said something similar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9701","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of winds, and he said Once again: On the authority of Riyah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ate food, he would say: “Praise be to God.” “Who has fed us and given us drink, and made us submissive.”"
"9702","Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Rabbati told me, he said: Al-Zubayri told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim Ismail bin Kathir, on the authority of Ismail bin Riyah, on the authority of Riyah bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say when he had finished His food: “Praise be to God who fed us, gave us drink, and made us Muslims.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9703","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Abdullah bin Muti’ told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ismail bin Idris, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that he used to say when he ate or drank: “Praise be to God who fed us, gave us drink, and made us Muslims.”"
"9704","Humayd bin Mukhlid bin Zanjawayh told me, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khumayr, On the authority of Abdullah bin Busr, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended upon him, and they brought him food, and he was eating dates. He places the stones on the back of his finger, then throws them away. He said: Then he got up riding a white mule of his, and I got up to take his ride, so I said: O Messenger of God, pray to God for us. He said: “O God, bless for them what You have provided for them, so forgive them, and have mercy on them.” Abu Dawud disagreed with him, and Bahz bin Asad disagreed with him."
"9705","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told me, he said: Abu Dawud told me, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Yazid bin Khumayr told me, saying: I heard Abdullah bin Busr says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended on my father, so my mother brought food to him, and he ate it, then dates were brought. So he started eating and saying the stones like this, and Abu Dawud brought his index and middle fingers together, turning them over to throw the stones, then he came. With a drink, he drank, then the one on his right gave it to him, and he said: Messenger of God, pray to God for us, and he said: “O God, bless them and provide for them. So forgive them and have mercy on them.” Amr bin Buraid Abu Burdah told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Yazid bin Khumayr told me, He said: I heard Abdullah bin Busr something similar."
"9706","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Hisham bin Yusuf told us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Busr speaking, That his father made food for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he called him and he answered him, and when he finished, he said: “O God, have mercy on them, forgive them, and bless for them in what You have provided for them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9707","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sarjis, he said: “I came to the Messenger of So I ate from his food, and I said: May God forgive you, O Messenger of God. He said: And for you. I said: I ask forgiveness for you. He said: Yes, and for you. So God said. God Almighty: And ask forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and believing women. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9708","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: That is, Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Anas He said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, broke his fast with a family, he would say: “The fasting people broke their fast with you, and the righteous ate your food.” And the angels descended upon you.”"
"9709","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, that Anas bin Malik narrated that when the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, broke his fast with a family, he would say: “May the fasting people break their fast with you, and eat Your food is the righteous, and the angels may bless you.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir did not hear it from Anas. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9710","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, informed us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: I narrated, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would break his fast with a family, he would say: “I will break my fast with you.” Those who fast, and the righteous eat your food.”"
"9711","Quraysh bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, he said: Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, he said: he told us Marwan Al-Muqaffa’, he said: I saw Ibn Umar seizing his beard and cutting off what exceeded the palm of his hand, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When he breaks his fast, he says: “The thirst has gone, the veins are moistened, and the reward is confirmed, God willing.”"
"9712","Yahya bin Muhammad bin Al-Sakan told us, he said: Yahya bin Kathir told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Al-Farra’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you is called, let him answer, but if he breaks the fast Let him eat, and if he is fasting, he should pray for blessing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9713","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Bishr bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Zuhair bin Muhammad, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A man from the Ansar from the people of Quba called for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so we set off with him, and when he ate and washed his hands Or his hands, he said: “Praise be to God who feeds and does not feed. Who has bestowed upon us, guided us, fed us, and given us drink, and caused us to do away with every good trial. Praise be to Him.” To God there is no deposit, no reward, no expiation, no place to be dispensed with. Praise be to God who provided food, gave drink water, and clothed people with food. Nudity, and guidance from error, and insight from blindness, and superiority over many of His creation. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9714","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, a recitation of it while I am listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, He said: Malik told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: When people saw the first fruit, they would bring it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. God bless him and grant him peace. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it, he said: “O God, bless our fruit for us, and bless our city. And bless for us our hardships, and bless our cities, O God, Abraham is your servant, your friend, and your prophet, and I am your servant and your prophet, and he is He invited you to Mecca, and I invite you to Medina in the same way as he called you in Mecca, and in the same way with him.” He said: Then he invites the youngest newborn he sees. So he gives him that fruit (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9715","Taliq bin Muhammad bin Al-Sakan told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Yazid bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abi Al-Jaad, On the authority of Aisha, she said: A sheep was given as a gift to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Divide it.” He said: When Aisha returned, The servant, she said: What did they tell you? You say what they say. He says: May God bless you. Then Aisha says: May God bless them. She responds to them as they said, and our reward remains ours. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9716","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hatim told us, on the authority of Salih bin Muhammad bin Zaida, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never raised his head to the sky except that he said: “O Converter of hearts, make my heart steadfast in your obedience.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9717","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Abu Amir told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Harith, and Al-Mundhir bin Abu Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at the moon and said: “O Aisha, seek refuge By God, from the evil of this, for when this darkness approaches, (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9718","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Al-Hafari told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took my hand, and when the moon rose, he said: “Seek refuge in God from the evil of this. \The dark one when he approaches\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9719","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Khalid told me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal On the authority of Al-Araj, he said: Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of a man from the Ansar, that he was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in He traveled and said: Let us see how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prays. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slept, then he woke up and raised He raised his head to the sky and recited four verses from the end of Surah Al Imran: Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth and in the alternation of night and day are signs for those of understanding. Until he passed by the four, then he put his hand in the closet and took a siwak and used it to cleanse himself, then he performed ablution and prayed, then he fell asleep, then he woke up and did Like what he did the first time, then he fell asleep, then he woke up and did what he did the first time, and they claim that it is the Tahajjud that God Almighty commanded to do.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9720","Muhammad bin Sahl bin Askar told us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, he said: Khallad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Khalid bin told me Abu Imran, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, never sat in a sitting room, nor did he recite the Qur’an. And he did not pray a single prayer without concluding that with words. She said: So I said: O Messenger of God, I see you not sitting in a seat, not reciting the Qur’an, nor praying a prayer. Didn't you conclude with these words? He said: “Yes, whoever says good, the mark of that good will be sealed for him, and whoever says evil, it will be an atonement for him: Glory be to You and praise be to You, there is no god but You.” “I ask your forgiveness and I repent to you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9721","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, he said: Saeed Abu Masoud told us Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, found a garment, he would name it by name. He said: “O God, you have clothed me in this garment, so praise be to You. I ask You for its goodness and the goodness of what was made for it, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of What was done to him.” Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak followed him, and Hammad bin Salamah opposed them."
"9722","Al-Hasan bin Ahmad bin Habib told us, he said: Ibrahim, who is the son of Al-Hajjaj, told us, he said: Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Alaa bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakheer, that whenever the Messenger of God put on a new garment, he would say: “O God, I ask you of His goodness and the goodness of what was done to him, and I seek refuge in You from his evil and the evil of what was done to him.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Hammad bin Salamah in Al-Jariri is more reliable than Isa bin Yunus, because Al-Jariri had mixed up, and Hammad bin heard A few drops of it before it was mixed. Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan said: He said in a whisper: We denounced Al-Jariri during the days of the plague, and a hadith Hammad is more deserving of the truth than the hadith of Jesus and Ibn Al-Mubarak, and God grant us success."
"9723","Nuh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Abdul Razzaq, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, saw a garment on Omar and said: “Is this new or washed?” He said: Washed. He said: “Wear new, live praiseworthy, and die a martyr.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith. Yahya bin Sa`id al-Qattan denied it to Abd al-Razzaq. They did not narrate it from anyone other than Mu`mar. Abdul Razzaq. This hadith was narrated on the authority of Maqil bin Abdullah, and there was disagreement over it. It was narrated on the authority of Maqil, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad. On the authority of Al-Zuhri, mursal, and this hadith is not from the hadith of Al-Zuhri, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9724","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Makhzoumi told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim told us, On the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib ibn Abi Al-Sa’ib, who was participating with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the pre-Islamic period. He said: The Messenger of God came to me. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “Welcome, my brother. He should not be ignored or shunned.”"
"9725","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Saeed bin Marwan al-Azdi from the people of Edessa told us, he said: Issam bin Bashir told us, he said: My father told me that Banu Al-Harith bin Ka’b sent him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So I entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I greeted him, and he said: “Hello, and peace be upon you. Where did you come from?” So I said: O Messenger of God, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. Banu Al-Harith came as a delegate to me. Welcome to Islam. He said: “Welcome to you. What is your name?” I said: “My name is Akbar.” He said: “Rather, you are good tidings.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called him Bashir. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9726","Abdah bin Abdullah told us, he said: Harami bin Hafs told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Muslim told us, he said: Yazid told us Ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, he said: The Ansar gathered, and they said: Go with us to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. And we ask Him to make our water flowing, for the springs have become too hard for us, and we have not asked Him for anything but He has given it to us, and He will not ask His Lord. He did not give it anything, so they came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he went out to them and said: “Welcome to the Ansar. He said it three times. Do not ask me.” “Today I have given nothing but that I have given you, and I do not ask my Lord but that He has given it to me.” So they left their question in which they had come, and said: O Messenger of God, call on God. Forgive us, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, forgive the Ansar, the sons of the Ansar, and the sons of the sons of the Ansar.”"
"9727","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr bin Abi Sufyan told me, that Amr bin Abd Allah ibn Safwan informed him, that Kalada ibn al-Hanbal informed him, that Safwan ibn Umayyah sent him to the Prophet, may God bless him, in the conquest. He greeted Laban, Giddaiah, and Dagabis, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was at the top of the valley. He said: So I entered upon him and did not greet him nor ask for permission. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Go back and say: Peace be upon you.” He said that after Safwan had converted to Islam. Amr said: Then he informed me. This news also came from Umayyah ibn Safwan, and Umayyah did not say: I heard it from Kalada. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9728","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of a man from Bani Amir. He asked permission to enter before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Shall I enter? So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Go out to him, for he does not know how to ask permission, so tell him: Let him say: Peace be upon you. Shall I come in?” So I heard him. He said that, so I said: Peace be upon you, shall I come in? He gave me permission and I entered (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9729","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith told us, he said: my father told us, he said: al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Saleel, on the authority of Abu Tamimah, on the authority of Jabir bin Sulaym, who said: I met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God. He said: “Peace be upon you, greeting the dead, peace be upon you” three times, that is, like this, so say"
"9730","Imran bin Yazid told me, he said: Isa told us, meaning Ibn Yunus, he said: Al-Muthanna Abu Ghaffar told us, he said: Abu Tamimah told us Al-Hujaimi, on the authority of Abu Jari, said: I came upon a man and the people around him did not utter anything except what he said, they did not utter anything he said, I said :Who is this? They said: This is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God, three times. He said: Do not say peace be upon you, for it is Greeting the dead, but say: Peace be upon you.”"
"9731","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Tamimah, on the authority of a man, he said: I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God. He said: “Peace be upon you is the greeting of the dead. When you meet your believing brother, say: Peace and God’s mercy be upon you.” And His blessings.” Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Tamimah, on the authority of a man, from his people, he said I looked for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but I was not able to find him, so I sat down, and behold, he departed. He was among them and I did not know him. When some of them rose up with him, They said: O Messenger of God, and when I saw that I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God, and the hadith was related to (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9732","Al-Fadl bin Sahl told us, he said: Al-Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Hassan bin Salih told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Omar said: “I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was drinking something, and I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God, peace be upon you. Will Omar enter? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9733","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Al-Hasan told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Sa’id. Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: Omar came and said: “Peace be upon the Messenger of God, peace be upon you. Will Omar enter?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9734","Muhammad ibn Hatim informed us, he said: Hibban informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Ibn Abu Laila, on the authority of Al-Miqdad ibn Al-Aswad, who said: I and a companion of mine came, and we began presenting ourselves to the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, and no one would accept us, so we came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his family brought us, and behold three goats, and the Prophet said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Milk this milk between us.” So we would milk it, and each person would drink his share, and we would raise it for the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he delivered his share. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would come in the middle of the night and greet him in a way that would not wake the sleeper but would make those who are awake hear. Then he would come. The mosque and he prays, then he brings his drink and drinks it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9735","Muhammad bin Ahmad told us, he said: Isa told us, meaning Ibn Yunus, he said: Ibn Abi Laila told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Asaad bin Zurarah, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Qais bin Saad bin Ubadah, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Saad, He said: “Peace be upon you.” Saad responded and was afraid. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw that he was not being called to prayer, he left, and Saad went after him. He said: O Messenger of God, nothing prevented me from hearing you except that I liked to greet you often. So he returned with him and put water for him in He washed himself, then he ordered a blanket dyed with rosemary and he wrapped himself in it, as if I were looking at the rosemary in the lining of his side. He said: O God, bless the Ansar and the descendants of the Ansar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
